TEXT 32 32 Left 3 ;#327 Basic PNP current mirror: ideal output-voltage sweep experiment
TEXT 32 96 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2IbWvq7Abv4
TEXT 32 144 Left 2 ;The same two-transistor mirror, with its collector voltage swept directly. The slope of the current shows Q2's finite output resistance (Early effect).
TEXT 32 672 Left 2 ;Vload replaces Alan's ammeter and adjustable load in this separate experiment. Vload sets Q2's collector voltage; I(Vload) is the output current.
TEXT 32 720 Left 2 !.dc Vload 0 11 0.1
TEXT 32 752 Left 2 !.meas dc I_AT_0V FIND I(Vload) AT=0
TEXT 32 784 Left 2 !.meas dc I_AT_5V FIND I(Vload) AT=5
TEXT 32 816 Left 2 !.meas dc ROUT_OHMS PARAM 5/(I_AT_0V-I_AT_5V)
